# scenarios/7_customer_deposit.books: loaded by ledger_server into 7_customer_deposit.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	7. A customer's deposit: money in, but no revenue yet
about	A deposit paid before the goods are delivered is not revenue: the company owes the goods, or the money back. It sits in Advances received, a liability (acomptes reçus, ontvangen vooruitbetalingen), until the delivery.
about	On delivery the whole 10,000 is invoiced and becomes revenue, and the deposit is set against the invoice: the customer owes only the 7,000 left.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Share capital
account	550000	asset	Bank
account	400000	asset	Trade receivables
account	460000	liability	Advances received
account	700000	revenue	Sales
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Share capital	-500000
posting	Bank	500000
entry	2011-02-01	The customer pays a 30% deposit on an order of 10,000
posting	Advances received	-300000
posting	Bank	300000
entry	2011-03-15	The goods are delivered and invoiced: 10,000
posting	Sales	-1000000
posting	Trade receivables	1000000
entry	2011-03-15	The deposit is set against the invoice
posting	Trade receivables	-300000
posting	Advances received	300000
entry	2011-04-15	The customer pays the 7,000 left
posting	Trade receivables	-700000
posting	Bank	700000
